{
  "requirement": "When a Bedrock configuration sets no `maxTokens` option, each provider request\nMUST ask for at most 16,384 output tokens. A configured `maxTokens` MUST be used\nas given.\n\nWhen a response stops because it reached a known output limit, the harness MUST\ncontinue the same conversation once, adding a user message with an error result\nfor each tool call in the cut-off response, followed by this text with `<limit>`\nreplaced by the limit:\n\n```text\nThe response was cut off at <limit> tokens. Continue with a shorter response and finish with submit_result.\n```\n\nA second response that reaches the limit, or a response that stops at an\noutput limit that is not known, MUST fail the assessment as an incomplete\nresponse. Where the provider reports whether a response stopped at the output\nlimit or because the conversation exceeded the model's context window, the\nharness SHOULD continue only the former and fail the assessment on the latter;\nwhere it does not, the stop MUST be treated as reaching the output limit.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover every obligation in `requirements.authoring.output_limit`.\n\n**Default limit.**\n- `providers.rs#mod[tests]/fn[bedrock_native_option_types_are_checked_and_only_max_tokens_is_defaulted]` asserts that `apply_bedrock_options` sets `max_tokens` to 16,384 when no `maxTokens` is configured.\n- `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[bedrock_requests_without_max_tokens_ask_for_at_most_16k_output_tokens]` asserts `inferenceConfig == {maxTokens:16384}` on every request, for two models.\n\n**Configured `maxTokens` used as given.**\n- `fn[bedrock_cli_uses_selected_profile_region_and_converse_tools]` asserts 321 in both requests.\n- `fn[a_configured_bedrock_limit_controls_requests_and_the_continuation_note]` asserts 321 on every request.\n\n**Continuation after a known limit.**\n- `fn[a_response_cut_off_at_the_output_limit_is_continued_once]` checks the following:\n  - The same conversation continues. The earlier messages are preserved, and the cut-off assistant turn is sent as it was.\n  - A single user message carries an error `toolResult` for each of the two cut-off tool calls, `cut` and `read-cut`.\n  - The note text follows those results, and it equals `LIMIT_NOTE`. The exact wording is \"The response was cut off at 16384 tokens. Continue with a shorter response and finish with submit_result.\"\n  - Exactly two attempts are made.\n- The `<limit>` substitution is checked with a configured Bedrock limit (321) and with an Ollama `num_predict` (512), in `fn[a_configured_bedrock_limit_controls_requests_and_the_continuation_note]` and `fn[a_configured_ollama_num_predict_is_the_known_output_limit]`.\n- The agent-level tests `fn[retries_and_cut_off_tools_preserve_inputs_and_submission_skips_other_reads]` and `fn[generic_conversations_can_use_default_telemetry_through_retry_and_continuation]` check that the cut-off tool calls get \"not run\" results and that the limit appears in the continuation.\n\n**Failure cases.**\n- A second response at the limit fails as incomplete: `fn[a_second_response_at_the_output_limit_fails_the_assessment]` asserts a non-zero exit, \"incomplete\" in stderr, and exactly two requests.\n- A stop at an output limit that is not known fails: `fn[a_stop_at_an_output_limit_that_is_not_known_fails_the_assessment]` uses Ollama with no `num_predict` and asserts failure with no continuation. `fn[truncation_without_a_provider_output_limit_fails_before_dispatch]` asserts an incomplete-response error and no dispatch.\n\n**Context window versus output limit (SHOULD).** `fn[a_context_window_overflow_fails_without_a_continuation]` uses a Bedrock `model_context_window_exceeded` stop. It asserts failure, \"context window\" in stderr, and no continuation request.\n\nWhere the provider does not distinguish the two stops, the stop is treated as reaching the output limit. The Ollama `length` reply is continued when the limit is known and failed when it is not, which covers that clause.\n\nI found no marking gap and no gap in the assertions.",
  "references": "bcfa912cbff6c6cbd139742810a1d59c670adfa381e9ac8e4eea28cc6942b586",
